/-!
# Finite data for the literal J₄ max1 action

The indices name the existing 16 × 8 × 8 Sylow transversal products.
The 192 vertices list all square-one elements; rows retain the original
eleven basis pairs and direct conjugation convention. The commutation bits and the two half-mask tables cache finite calculations.
The latter give the displacement of each low six-bit or high five-bit mask.
These are data only, checked in the block modules.
Source: ATLAS J4G1-max1W1 and the pair-label tables in `Image.StarData`.
-/
@[expose] public noncomputable section
namespace Janko4.TwoRank.Finite
open LocalStructure.SylowCore LocalStructure.SylowCore.FiniteBoundCertificate
open LocalStructure.SylowCore.FiniteBoundCertificate.NormalWeights

@[reducible] def Table (α : Type) : ℕ → Type
  | 0 => α
  | n + 1 => Table α n × Table α n
def lookup {α : Type} : (n : ℕ) → Table α n → ℕ → α
  | 0, t, _ => t
  | n + 1, t, i => lookup n (if i % 2 = 0 then t.1 else t.2) (i / 2)

